---
title: Pan-Fried Venison with Port and Plum Sauce
description: Seared rich game meat with a deep fruity sauce
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/pan-fried-venison-sloe-gin-plum-sauce
author: Sara Buenfeld
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/venison-de884d3.jpg?quality=90&webp=true&resize=440,400
servings: 2
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 15m
cook time: 25m 
course: Main
cuisine: British
tags:
- savoury
- main-course
- meat
- british
---

Press the @juniper berries{6}(finely chopped) and lots of @black pepper{}(freshly ground) onto the @venison steaks{2}. Heat the @butter{15%g} in a #frying pan{} until foaming, then add the @plums{2}(quartered) quarters and steaks. Cook for about ~{15%minutes}, turning halfway through. Remove and keep warm.

Tip the @plum{1}(finely chopped) and @garlic{1%clove}(finely chopped) into the pan juices and cook, stirring, until softened. Pour in the @port{2%tsp} and allow to sizzle, then add the @hot beef stock{125%ml}.

Put the steaks on warmed plates, top with the plum quarters and spoon round some sauce. Scatter over the @thyme sprigs{} and a little black pepper.